From: Bryan Roscoe <bryanroscoe@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 21:05:04 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 24/30] Parser: "<permanents> can't have <kind> counters put on
 them"

Darksteel Angel (and Melira, Sylvok Outcast): "Creatures you control
can't have -1/-1 counters put on them."

CR 614.17 + CR 614.6 + CR 122.1: a counter-placement prohibition is an
AddCounter event that never happens. phase models "can't have counters
put on" lines that way (Solemnity, Melira's Keepers), but this form
names a counter kind, so the classifier didn't route it to the
replacement parser and it failed the static parser: -1/-1 counters were
still put on the controller's creatures.

The classifier now recognizes "can't have <kind> counters put on", and
the replacement parser lowers "<type phrase> can't have <kind> counters
put on them" to the AddCounter prevention scoped to the subject (its
controller included) and to that counter kind (counter_match), so other
counters are still put on them.

Test: oracle_replacement tests
counter_kind_prohibition_scopes_subject_and_kind.

Card data: reaches games only with card data generated by this parser.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 crates/engine/src/parser/oracle_classifier.rs | 15 ++++-
 .../engine/src/parser/oracle_replacement.rs   | 58 +++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 70 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

